  <section class="section wrap" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <h2 id="method-title">How the AI involvement scale works</h2>
        <p>Each level needs reviewable evidence. Games stay unrated until enough has been checked.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="scale">
      <li style="--lvl:#c9d2df"><span class="lvl">0</span><span class="desc">No evidence found. Not proof of no AI.</span></li>
      <li style="--lvl:#f3d9a6"><span class="lvl">1</span><span class="desc">Used as a development or marketing aid</span></li>
      <li style="--lvl:#ecbd6c"><span class="lvl">2</span><span class="desc">Limited in-game assets</span></li>
      <li style="--lvl:#de9a32"><span class="lvl">3</span><span class="desc">Assets across several in-game categories</span></li>
      <li style="--lvl:#bf7410"><span class="lvl">4</span><span class="desc">A major production component</span></li>
      <li style="--lvl:#8a4a00"><span class="lvl">5</span><span class="desc">Runs at play time or is a core mechanic</span></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="scale-note">
      <p>Official disclosures, reviewed third-party evidence and unverified community reports are always labeled separately. Level 0 is not a certification of zero AI use.</p>
      <p>Reporting a game? Include a source URL, its date, the affected content and context.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

